+# Bug Fix: Category deletion removes products and breaks references
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Category deletion now removes only product-category join rows for the complete stored subtree and never deletes products. Descendant discovery uses the category lineage prefix, so child memberships are removed before the category hierarchy is deleted.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java` | modified | Retains products, collects the full subtree, and removes only category memberships. |
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/catalog/category/CategoryRepository.java` | modified | Adds a transactional bulk cleanup of `PRODUCT_CATEGORY` rows. |
+| `sm-core/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/catalog/CategoryTest.java` | modified | Adds parent/child, product-retention, and surviving-category regression coverage. |
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- `CategoryTest.deleteCategoryKeepsProductsAndRemovesDeletedTreeMemberships` — verifies products survive while deleted-tree memberships are removed and surviving memberships remain.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-core -am -Dtest=CategoryTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed; 2 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors.
+- Manual checks: `git diff --check` passed.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The preferred remediation was expanded to include a repository-level transactional join-table cleanup after the initial collection-only update failed the FK regression test. Descendant collection was also corrected to use the stored lineage prefix because the previous root-id concatenation omitted descendants.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Run the shop integration/API suite against the application service to verify HTTP 404 and cart/order flows end to end.
